From ae595da8c2b67f23939a535de0961aaae4486490 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:02:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Gather: relocate to 5 mesh-valid spots within 50 yd before
 giving up on a hotspot

When a hotspot leg failed (key-steered walk stalled ~16 yd away and every
sidestep was refused because the short ray hit the mesh edge), the gatherer
retried the same leg from the same spot three times and stopped.

Now a failed hotspot leg triggers up to 5 relocations: pick a mesh-valid,
reachable point within 50 yd of the character (spread across directions, safe
area type, outside profile blackspots, complete validated path), walk to it,
then ask for the hotspot again from there. Only after all 5 fail does the
gatherer stop. Roaming mode still just counts the failure and picks a new
random destination.

Adds MeshRelocate (sampler + self-test), exposes MeshRoam.SafeDestinationArea.
---
 .../Pathing/ClickAim/ClickAimDiagnostics.cs   |   3 +
 Styx/Logic/Pathing/ClickAim/GatherRunner.cs   |  67 ++++++++
 Styx/Logic/Pathing/ClickAim/MeshRelocate.cs   | 159 ++++++++++++++++++
 Styx/Logic/Pathing/ClickAim/MeshRoam.cs       |   2 +-
 4 files changed, 230 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 Styx/Logic/Pathing/ClickAim/MeshRelocate.cs

